{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/582185-where-did-the-non-ghost-inhabitants-of-the-shadowlands-tempest-labyrinth-come-from","id":582185,"title":"Where did the non-ghost inhabitants of the Shadowlands/Tempest/Labyrinth come from?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-07T06:04:01-07:00","id":582185,"title":"Where did the non-ghost inhabitants of the Shadowlands/Tempest/Labyrinth come from?","content":"There are lots of non-Wraith/Spectre inhabitants of the Lands of The Dead, starting with the things in the Tempest, and ending with all the flora of the Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> Since, more or less as a rule, everything across the Shroud is made up of dead people, or memories thereof, where did plasmics come from? Are they some sort of idea/memory given from of plasm? Are they dead dogs, pardon the banality?<br /> <br /> I tend to view Wraith as a total standalone, as it mixes rather badly with the rest of WoD (and should not be mixed, imho), so this is a sticking point to me.<br /> <br /> Do you, forumites, have any ideas? Is there any Deadguy-approved answer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T07:47:15-07:00","id":583460,"title":"","content":"I normally go with the idea/memory given form like some kind of dark-umbra version of a chimeric creation for Plasmics but I don't limit beings in the shadowlands only to plasms and Wraiths/Spectres. Anything that has died a particularly horrible death can end up their as shown in dead animals per Orpheus or even the last Ancestor Spirit of the White Howlers per the W20: Umbra book. Changeling had a creature that came into existence when the spirit of someone who died was carried into the Dreaming so its plausible that other spirits could wander the other way and get lost in the storm. The Silent Striders, Black Spiral Dancers, and members of the Hengeyokai are known for traveling into the Lands of the Dead more frequently then the other but any member of the Fera could potentially cross into the Dark Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T09:29:36-07:00","id":583543,"title":"","content":"If you go by Orpheus, plasmics could have started as the metaphysical equivalent of Grandmother's discards.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the Kraken's existence suggests there's a realm beyond the Tempest where the Kraken is bound. How was the Kraken contained? And what else, if anything, might that realm contain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:44:27-07:00","id":583628,"title":"","content":"I've always viewed the Kraken as not so much bound as some weird alien thing beyond life or death that only occasionally finds rifts in the fabric of the Underworld that it can reach in through when the stars are right. More H.P. Lovecraft than August Derleth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T05:24:49-07:00","id":584573,"title":"","content":"Plasmics can more properly be imagined as manifestations of the chaos of the Tempest. They're entropic madness and emotion given form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T05:39:47-07:00","id":584582,"title":"","content":"Well there are a couple of answers that hinge on the Underworld being the Low Umbra, but since you don't want to bring other games into it, I will leave them out. Here are some other possibilities:<br /> <br /> - It could be that some relics, as they are forgotten lose their form but not the emotional investment, becoming ambulatory but not quite coherent forms.<br /> <br /> -They could be the relics of strong shared ideas, such as the thrill of the hunt or the sweetness of revenge. If animals could invest enough emotional energy to create relics, these would be the kind they created.<br /> <br /> - They could be the remnants of Wraiths who degraded impossibly long ago, before Oblivion was strong enough to corrupt the process. They lost their identities and their wills, but they never fell to their own self destructive impulses. <br /> <br /> - They could be drones and blips from long ago that somehow learned new (albeit primitive) Passions.<br /> <br /> - They could be the remnants of dead dreams, ideals, and broken promises.<br /> <br /> - Finally, the Underworld is a strange and mysterious place that has its own shadow ecology. Strange things that could never exist on earth arise there through unknowable processes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T16:56:33-07:00","id":589651,"title":"","content":"The above answers work well enough within the <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> 'canon' scheme of things. There are a couple of other options that one <i>might</i> consider, at varying degrees of separation from <b>Wraith</b>...<br /> <br /> First, the description of how the Underworld came to be that's offered in <b>Demon: the Fallen</b> suggest that when the angel Charon (NOT the same bloke we know as the lord of Stygia, but possibly the archetype on which the later Charon based himself) found/created/manifested that realm which became the Underworld, it was a perfect mirror of the living world. That is, it had plants and animals and mountains and everything. When the Tempest grew out of Charon's mirror world, it left what we know as the Shadowlands, but the deeper Underworld took with it bits of the first incarnation. Hence, all manner of things that don't QUITE pass for 'ghosts' made it into the Underworld, and since they'd always been there (again, from the wonky, timey-wimey 'history' of <b>Demon</b>, such as it is), they shall ever be there.<br /> <br /> Second\u2014and likely much more controversial on this forum board\u2014is the take on the Underworld from <b>Exalted</b>, especially from the books regarding the Abyssal Exalted. In that version, when the catastrophic war with the Primordials (think of them as the Titans from Greek Mythology pumped up on steroids and living in a heavenly version of every Las Vegas Casino) ended with some of those self-same Primodials dying, that unfathomable event created the Underworld. Those dead Primordials retained some shards of their souls (no, I won't go into the mechanics of it), and their palace-tombs fell towards the perfection of Oblivion. Spoiler alert! They became the Neverborn. Anyways, around them grew a reflection of Creation, where all of the features existed in distorted ways. That included animals, plants, and other <i>things</i>, along with places for ghosts. Reflections of anything from Creation were twisted, or the servants of the Neverborn made their own twisted mockeries of Creation's denizens, and that's were the plasmics came from.<br /> <br /> ...Now, like I said, these are NOT <b>Wraith</b> in origin, but to my way of looking at the Underworld, they are fine possible explanations if taken with grains of salt.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: I had a flood at home, and my books are all locked away from the water-logged rooms (none of them were damaged, in case you worry), so I may have some of the details on both of the above off the mark. Forgive and feel free to amend/ignore/berate if that's the case!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T09:38:55-07:00","id":590268,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I go with the above post. The link between Exalted and owod was clearer before the time of Demon came about and by then the Wraith line was done with. To me the Primordials are the <i>original</i> Malfeans, the Neverborn, the Grotesques. The Isle of Sorrows always seemed to me to be the same Isle of Sytgia that was the mirror of the Blessed Isle in Creation, as the Venous Star is the pit to Oblivion mirroring the immense mountain in Creation.<br /> <br /> How this links into the rather Judeo-Christian take being fact that Demon and later owod went with (outside of the Kindred of the East) I'm not sure on. However mention was given to the Scarlet Pheonix and Ebon Dragon being the last living Angels, both of which are named characters in Exalted, the latter being a Primordial.<br /> <br /> Wyrds, Deliriums and Legendaries do make me think that some remnants of memories or perception in the mind (Umbra links) are occuring also, just because the xenomorph from ALIEN was mentioned as a Wyrd in the book 'Sea of Shadows'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T19:58:43-07:00","id":590716,"title":"","content":"Some books hint that the Underworld was not always separate, that the spiritual realms and the physical plane were one. The flora and fauna of the Underworld were probably &quot;walled off&quot; by the growing and strengthening Shroud along with the rest of the Shadowlands during this time. So, in a sense, they're natural. Others are, as has been noted, psychic flotsam given agency - the Tempest being images and emotion, a few independent actors are bound to emerge.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 07-14-2015, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T02:23:34-07:00","id":591027,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the replies, that gives me some nice creepy stuff to work with. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}